      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Hide the resume prompt once resume is queued**\n\nWhen an offline resume from `ResumeTrackingPrompt` is queued and the app restarts before synchronization, the hydrated pause query still says the pause is active because this prompt's success handler never projects the queued resume into that cache. The prompt therefore reappears and this path queues a second resume behind the first; replaying the first clears the active pause, then the second receives the backend's non-retryable `NO_ACTIVE_PAUSE` 409 and becomes a permanent outbox barrier. Overlay pending resume intent in the prompt or persist an inactive pause snapshot when the first resume is queued.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
